-- title:
--   Finite level sets of Ogg's unit with linear rank bound
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \ne 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $N_0q$, and let $A =$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` be the finite-$j$ chart algebra: the subalgebra of $F$, over the base ring `R q` $= \mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$ (rationals with denominator prime to $q$), consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$-subalgebra generated by $j$ (`IgusaScheme.jFull`), i.e. the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}[j]$ in $F$. Let $v \in A$ be an element whose $\mathfrak q$-expansion, as a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, is either `modularUnitSeries q` $= \Delta(\mathfrak q)\,\Delta(\mathfrak q^{q})^{-1}$ or the product of the constant series $q^{12}$ with the inverse of that series. The assertion is that there exists $K \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose constant coefficient is not divisible by $q$, the quotient of $A$ by the ideal generated by $g(v)$ is a finite $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$-module and its `Module.finrank` over $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$ is at most $K \cdot \deg g$. The constant $K$ is uniform in $g$.
--
--   This is the finiteness statement, with a linear bound in $\deg g$, for level sets of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(q\tau)$ on the finite-$j$ chart of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$. It supplies the finiteness and upper rank bound used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval).
